`<changed_files>` is a JSON array of repository-relative paths. The diff is not inlined. Run ONE batched command to get the full diff for every changed file at once:

```
git diff 'origin/{{ base_ref }}' HEAD
```

Do NOT run a separate `git diff` per file; one batched command keeps the review fast and avoids dozens of redundant tool calls. To narrow the diff to specific paths, append `-- '<path>' '<path>' ...` using paths copied verbatim from `<changed_files>`. Use TWO refs separated by a space (`'origin/{{ base_ref }}' HEAD`), NOT the three-dot `...` form: the review checkout is a shallow merge commit with no shared history, so a three-dot/merge-base diff fails. Wrap the ref and every path in single quotes so the shell cannot split, glob, or interpret them; refs and paths can contain shell metacharacters. If a value itself contains a literal single quote, escape it as `'\''`. Never interpolate, concatenate, or word-split these values into the command.

